            "lens": "review-resilience",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 26 manifest paths for failure handling, retry safety, graceful degradation, latency and load. I found no concrete candidate-caused production failure mode.",
              "In engine/synctrigger/synctrigger.go, rotateLog is best effort. It takes the lock only when the log is full, rechecks the size under it, and returns without rotating if the lock or a rename fails. The log then keeps growing until the next open, and the sync is never blocked.",
              "The shift loop stops at the first rename failure that is not a missing file, so no rename can land on an older file that was not moved out of the way. engine/synctrigger/hardening_test.go pins this with a non-empty .3 directory.",
              "A trigger that opened the log before a rotation keeps writing through its descriptor, so its lines land in .1 and none is lost. A test pins this.",
              "boundedBuffer in engine/synctrigger/synctrigger.go reports full writes, so io.MultiWriter does not short-write and the log still gets all output. The child's memory use is capped at 64 KiB.",
              "A non-absolute state directory is refused in openLog and in RunChild, which returns skip:no-binary. The golden engine/cmd/testdata/synctrigger-golden/no-home-and-no-state-directory-writes-nothing.golden shows exit 0, an error:log line on stderr and nothing written, so the always-exit-0 contract holds. The base wrote the log under the working directory in this case.",
              "The 0644 to 0600 log mode change and the new no-HOME golden are what the task requested. The remaining files are receipts, task notes and a comment edit, with no runtime effect."
            ]
          }
        }
