            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "engine/synctrigger/synctrigger.go: rotateLog checks the size, takes the filelock, then re-checks the size. A missing file reads as not full, so the window between rename and reopen is safe. A shift that fails other than with ErrNotExist stops the rotation before any rename could overwrite a file. All of this is best effort and never changes the always-exit-0 contract.",
              "engine/synctrigger/hardening_test.go covers the behaviors from outside: rotation keeping three older files, 16 concurrent triggers over 20 rounds, a descriptor opened before a rotation, a failed shift (a non-empty directory at .3), 0600 narrowing of an existing 0644 log, field quoting, both sides of the 64 KiB stderr bound, and a relative state directory writing nothing and running nothing.",
              "boundedBuffer.Write reports len(p), so io.MultiWriter does not short-write and the log still receives all stderr output. RunChild returns skip:no-binary for a non-absolute state directory when no binary is given, so no default binary is run from a relative path.",
              "The new golden no-home-and-no-state-directory-writes-nothing.golden shows exit 0, an error:log line on stderr and an empty directory. The other golden changes are only the log mode from 0644 to 0600, which the task asked for.",
              "The receipts and task markdown record state and documentation only and have no runtime effect. The edit to the binaryIdentity comment in engine/status/status.go changes no behavior."
            ]
          }
